<h2 class="font-headline-lg text-headline-md lg:text-headline-lg text-on-surface font-bold tracking-tight">
            From Grassroots Founders to a National Federation
          </h2>
<p class="font-body-lg text-body-md lg:text-body-lg text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed">
            FLAME PH began with a profound, undeniable reality: over 99.5% of business establishments in the Philippines are classified as micro, small, and medium enterprises, yet they remain the most vulnerable to regulatory friction, supply chain disruption, and unfair financial middlemen.
          </p>
<p class="font-body-md text-body-md text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed">
            Originally incorporated as <strong class="text-on-surface font-bold">FAME PH (Founders' Association of MSMEs and Entrepreneurs, Inc.)</strong> under the Securities and Exchange Commission, our movement brought together street-level merchants, provincial artisans, agri-cooperatives, and tech-forward store owners. As our provincial networks expanded from a dozen pioneering chapters into an archipelago-wide network, the organization matured into <strong class="text-primary font-bold">FLAME PH (Federation of Leaders Advancing MSME Ecosystem in the Philippines)</strong>.
          </p>
<div class="p-space-md bg-surface-container rounded-xl flex items-start gap-space-md">
